# Independent operational repos nested in the realm. Each is its own git repo (or plain dir);
# the realm fork tracks only the governance machinery (CASE-LAW, VPR, court/, caselaw/) + the
# realm structure (ministries, signposts, the ledger), never the departments' contents.
/ministry-for-business-work-and-skills/engineering-department/projects/
/ministry-for-business-work-and-skills/legal-department/harvey-labs/
/ministry-for-business-work-and-skills/legal-department/references/
/ministry-for-business-work-and-skills/skills-and-education/scratch-to-signals/
/ministry-for-business-work-and-skills/business-operations/Clara/
/national-archives/

# Ministry of Security operational estate registry - PRIVATE (holds the facts: the master digital
# estate registry, the repo->server-config list, and policy papers). The public law (REALM-SI 1)
# states principles only; the facts never enter the public tree. (Provisional name pending the
# Ministry rename; consolidates with the security ministry.)
/ministry-of-security/

# Secrets and build artefacts - never commit
**/node_modules/
**/.env
.env
*.env.local
law-reports/node_modules/
law-reports/review-service/node_modules/
law-reports/review-service/data/

# OS / editor junk - never belongs in the repo (and never in a public VJS)
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*
**/._*
*.swp
Thumbs.db
